# Device hostname
# Read by scripts/common_functions.sh at boot to set /proc/sys/kernel/hostname.
#
# The hostname appears in syslog messages, mDNS/Avahi (if enabled), and
# ONVIF device discovery responses.  Keep it short, alphanumeric + hyphens.
#
# Example: TC100-Living-Room
#
# Give EACH camera a unique hostname: the MQTT bridge derives its client id and
# topic root from this name when they are left at their defaults, so a unique
# hostname is what keeps two cameras from colliding as one device in Home
# Assistant. Set it in the first-boot wizard or the Network tab.
TC100-CAMERA
